# Configuration example

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is git-ignored; this example is committed
and must never contain a real secret.

`scripts/run-api.sh` sources `.env` automatically before starting the API.

---

## Database

Must point at a database **separate from the legacy `LegacyEcommerceDb`**.

```bash
# Used by docker-compose.dev.yml.
SHOPHUB_DB_PASSWORD='<your-strong-password>'

# Local Docker container started on port 1434 (see README section 4.1)
SHOPHUB_DB_CONNECTION='Server=localhost,1434;Database=ShopHubModernDb;User Id=sa;Password=<your-strong-password>;TrustServerCertificate=True;MultipleActiveResultSets=True'

# Or an existing SQL Server Express instance
# SHOPHUB_DB_CONNECTION='Server=localhost;Database=ShopHubModernDb;User Id=sa;Password=<your-password>;TrustServerCertificate=True'

# Or LocalDB (no credentials)
# SHOPHUB_DB_CONNECTION='Server=(localdb)\MSSQLLocalDB;Database=ShopHubModernDb;Trusted_Connection=True'
```

## API

```bash
# Where the API listens.
SHOPHUB_API_URL='http://localhost:5099'

# Trusted frontend origins. Only these may call the API cross-origin.
SHOPHUB_CORS_ORIGIN='http://localhost:5173'

# JWT issuer / audience.
SHOPHUB_JWT_ISSUER='ShopHubApi'
SHOPHUB_JWT_AUDIENCE='ShopHubClient'

# HMAC signing key. MUST be at least 32 characters; the API refuses to start otherwise.
# Generate one with:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
SHOPHUB_JWT_SIGNINGKEY='<at-least-32-random-characters>'
```

## Rate limiting

`.env` holds the `SHOPHUB_*` names below. `scripts/run-api.sh` maps them onto the
`RateLimiting:*` configuration keys the application actually reads
(`RateLimiting__Enabled`, `RateLimiting__AuthPermitLimit`, `RateLimiting__GlobalPermitLimit`).

```bash
SHOPHUB_RATE_LIMITING='true'      # set to false only for load testing
SHOPHUB_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT='10'      # requests per minute per IP on /api/auth/*
SHOPHUB_GLOBAL_RATE_LIMIT='300'   # requests per minute per IP everywhere
```

`scripts/run-api-e2e.sh` raises both limits for the Playwright suite, which drives many
requests from a single IP.

## Seeded accounts (development only)

```bash
SHOPHUB_SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL='admin@shophub.local'
SHOPHUB_SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD='<development-password>'
SHOPHUB_SEED_CUSTOMER_EMAIL='customer@shophub.local'
SHOPHUB_SEED_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD='<development-password>'
```

---

## Equivalent .NET configuration

Any of the above can be supplied directly as environment variables instead:

```bash
export ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection='Server=localhost,1434;Database=ShopHubModernDb;...'
export Jwt__Issuer='ShopHubApi'
export Jwt__Audience='ShopHubClient'
export Jwt__SigningKey='<at-least-32-random-characters>'
export Jwt__AccessTokenMinutes='15'
export Jwt__RefreshTokenDays='7'
export Cors__AllowedOrigins__0='http://localhost:5173'
export RateLimiting__Enabled='true'
```

Or through user secrets (never committed):

```bash
cd backend
dotnet user-secrets --project Ecommerce.Api set "Jwt:SigningKey" "<your-key>"
dotnet user-secrets --project Ecommerce.Api set "ConnectionStrings:DefaultConnection" "<your-connection-string>"
```
